WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.204
PROTESTERS GATHERED IN ARIZONA
THIS WEEKEND TO PROTEST AND CAST

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:07.307
DOUBT ON THE LEGITIMACY OF THE
ELECTORAL PROCESS THERE.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.109
WHY?
BECAUSE THEIR CANDIDATE IS

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.977
LOSING.
&gt;&gt; I BELIEVE AT THIS POINT WE

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:14.747
NEED TO JUST HAVE A NEW ELECTION
AT THIS POINT AND WE NEED TO DO

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:19.852
PAPER BALLOTS AND DO IT ALL IN
ONE DAY AND BE DONE WITH IT.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:22.455
IT'S AN ABSURD NOTION TO PLAY
THE CHARADE AND ACT LIKE AFTER

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:25.992
THIS COUNTING WE WON'T HAVE
TAINTED RESULTS EITHER WAY.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:32.298
&gt;&gt; BUT DEMOCRACY IS NOT A STATIC
THING AS WE KNOW, IT LIVES AND

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:35.635
BREATHES AND MUST CONSTANTLY BE
DEFENDED AGAINST THOSE WHO WOULD

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.905
DESTROY IT.
WE'RE STILL A YOUNG COUNTRY AND

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:42.275
ON NOVEMBER 8th MILLIONS OF
AMERICANS WENT TO THE POLLS AND

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:45.979
DID THAT.
A LOT OF FOLKS GOT IT WRONG.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:51.117
SO HOW DID THE PUNDITS AND POLL
WATCHERS GET IT SO WRONG?

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:58.391
ONE OF THEM HERE IS FRANK LUNTZ,
HE TWEETED OUT, WHEN THE DUST

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:05.098
SETTLES THE GOP WILL HAVE
BETWEEN 223, 230 HOUSE SEATS.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.734
REPUBLICANS WILL ALSO TAKE
CONTROL OF THE SENATE.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:13.406
LET'S BRING IN THE MAN BEHIND
THAT TWEET MR. FRANK LUNTZ.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.042
&gt;&gt; AND I ACKNOWLEDGED ON TWEETS
SINCE THEN.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.945
I DON'T SEE ANY POLLSTERS
SHOWING UP.

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.014
WHERE ARE YOU?
&gt;&gt; YOU ARE.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:24.150
HOW DID SO MANY PEOPLE,
INCLUDING YOU, GET IT SO WRONG?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.054
AS I SAID IN THE BEGINNING
THERE, WE TEND TO OVERINDEX,

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:33.059
WE'VE BEEN DOING IT SINCE 2016,
OVER INDEXING THE MAGA PART OF

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:36.629
THE ELECTORATE.
&gt;&gt; THERE'S A FEAR THEY DID NOT

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.632
INCLUDE ENOUGH REPUBLICANS IN
THEIR SAMPLES.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:43.503
BECAUSE WE KNEW FROM 2016, 2018,
AND 2020, THAT TRUMP VOTERS

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.739
TENDED NOT TO RESPOND TO
POLLSTERS BECAUSE THEY THOUGHT

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.809
THE RESULTS WOULD BE USED
AGAINST THEM.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:55.114
THERE'S AN EFFORT TO, AS YOU
SAY, OVER INDEX, THAT'S NUMBER

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:58.218
ONE.
NUMBER TWO PEOPLE CAME TO THE

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:03.189
POLLS AND DECIDED ENOUGH IS
ENOUGH.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:08.261
ABOUT 8% COMES IN UNDECIDED AND
HAS TO DECIDE AT THAT MOMENT.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.064
THEY WANT TO VOTE ONE WAY AND
END UP VOTING THE OTHER.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.499
&gt;&gt; WHAT DO YOU MEAN BY THAT?
&gt;&gt; Reporter: THEY COME IN AND

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.602
THINK I'M GOING TO VOTE
REPUBLICAN.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:19.539
AND THEN THEY GO AND HAVE TO
DECIDE DO THEY PULL THE BALLOTS

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:24.176
OR DO THEY WANT TO MAKE A
STATEMENT BY VOTING DEMOCRAT?

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:28.081
8% OF THE POPULATION COMES IN
AND MAY CHANGE THEIR MINDS.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.583
THIRD IS THAT THE INDEPENDENTS,
AND THIS IS WHERE THE

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:35.221
REPUBLICANS HAVE TO TAKE VERY
CLOSE ANALYSIS TO.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:39.692
THE INDEPENDENTS USUALLY BREAK
55/45 REPUBLICAN.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:43.763
IF THEY BREAK 60/40, REPUBLICANS
WIN.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:47.634
IN THIS CASE THEY BROKE 50/50.
THAT'S A REAL PROBLEM FOR THE

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.868
GOP.
IT'S A DROP.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.772
AND ONE MORE, REPUBLICANS GOT 5
MILLION MORE VOTES FOR THE HOUSE

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.774
THAN THE DEMOCRATS.
5 MILLION.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:58.578
SO WHY DON'T THE RESULTS SHOW
THEMSELVES IN THE CONGRESSIONAL

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.847
RACES?
THE ANSWER, REDISTRICTING.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:06.052
THAT HAD A BIGGER IMPACT AGAINST
THE GOP THAN ANYBODY REALIZED

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.855
AND YOU COULD NOT KNOW THIS
UNTIL ELECTION DAY.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:11.090
&gt;&gt; YOU BROUGHT UP INDEPENDENTS,
RIGHT.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:17.163
AND ONE OF THE SPLITS WAS 49/47,
YOU SAID 50/50, BUT WE GET THE

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.598
GIST.
"THE WASHINGTON JOURNAL"

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:21.167
EDITORIAL BOARD WRITES THE
MESSAGE COULDN'T BE CLEARER,

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.469
INDEPENDENT VOTERS MAY BE
UNHAPPY WITH THE DIRECTION OF

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:26.673
THE COUNTRY BUT THEY DIDN'T
TRUST THE GOP ENOUGH TO GIVE

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.941
